=== PARITY (vs web SecurityStatusWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (SecuritySource -> SecurityModel):
    useVehicles, useSecurityLatest, useTranslation. The production app wires SecuritySource over the
    KMP `security/latest` query store; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> SecurityCellsBuilder.build is a 1:1 port of the web `cells` useMemo:
    [lock]    locked ? ok/"Locked"(lock.fill) : error/"Unlocked"(lock.open.fill)
    [sentry]  sentry_mode ? ok/"Active"(checkmark.shield.fill) : inactive/"Off"(shield.fill)
    [doors]   open-door count == 0 ? ok/"All Closed" : warning/"<n> Open"   (door.left.hand.open)
    [windows] open-window count == 0 ? ok/"All Closed" : warning/"<n> Open" (macwindow)
    Returns [] when there is no event (web `if (!securityData) return []`) -> grid empty state.
  Door/window parsing -> SecuritySignalParser faithfully reproduces the web logic and is asserted by
    EXECUTED tests: door_state === true -> 1 open; comma-string -> split/trim/drop-empty/filter
    lowercase contains "open"; a window is open when boolean true OR a non-empty string != "closed"
    (case-insensitive); empty/absent -> closed. The string|boolean|null union (raw signal.SignalValue)
    is modeled as SecuritySignalValue {boolean|text|absent} and type-narrowed like the web `typeof`.
  Composition -> shell chrome (green shield icon + "Security" title + freshness chip + refresh + Open) ·
    fixed 2-column status grid (web cols={2}) of 4 tinted cells, each with a corner status dot, leading
    SF Symbol, muted label + emphasized value · grid-level empty state ("No security data").
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone / TSSkeleton +
    ContentUnavailableView, compiled against the REAL apps/apple design system in the SDK typechecks
    below. Cell tinting reproduces the web statusStyles table (ok=emerald, warning=amber, error=red,
    inactive/unknown=neutral). Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton 2x2 grid) · empty ("No security data") · error (retry
    affordance) · stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached value + chip + banner) · content. Model phase
    resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web shell.
  i18n -> all 12 web source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.security, lock, locked, unlocked, sentry, active, off, doors, windows, allClosed, open,
    noSecurity -> ALL PRESENT in SecurityStatusWidget.strings (+ registry description, freshness/refresh/
    retry/empty/error chrome, and a11y status words). No English literals in native code (verbatim facade).
  a11y -> each cell carries a combined "<label>, <value>, <status>" label; the grid a combined summary;
    every button an accessibilityLabel; status dots/icons accessibilityHidden; Dynamic Type via tokens;
    Reduce Motion gates the TSSkeleton shimmer.
  Telemetry -> SecurityModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"SecurityStatusWidget") -> bridges the
    shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (fires exactly once).
  Registry -> SecurityStatusWidget.registration: id "security-status", category "security", default 1x2,
